# Lore drafts (canon: soft): places in and beyond the academy.

@lore the_village
keys: village, barge, market square
canon: soft
text: The village lies across the lake, reached by barge. Its shopkeepers have seen every kind of student: the Gilded Newt, Mabel's tea shop, Grimsby's Books, Pell & Daughters and the bakery.

@lore gilded_newt
keys: Gilded Newt, tavern
canon: soft
text: The village tavern, with low beams and a fire that never goes out. Students work shifts there and card games run late.

@lore mabels
keys: Mabel's, tea shop
canon: soft
text: Forty kinds of tea and three kinds of cake. Mabel reads your mood from the way you open the door.

@lore grimsbys
keys: Grimsby's Books, bookshop
canon: soft
text: A bookshop so crowded the shelves lean on each other. Mr Grimsby will find anything except what you came in for.

@lore pell_and_daughters
keys: Pell & Daughters, apothecary, Old Pell
canon: soft
text: The village apothecary, with a thousand labelled drawers. Old Pell taught three generations to count drops.

@lore bakery
keys: bakery, baker's daughter
canon: soft
text: The same family has baked in the village for two hundred years. A great-great-great-grandmother waited all her life for a letter from a student who died.

@lore whisperwood
keys: Whisperwood, forest, moonpetal, shadow stag
canon: soft
text: An old forest west of the lake that talks in its sleep. Moonpetal blooms in its clearings only at midnight; a stag made of shadow guards them and steps aside only for the brave.

@lore secret_garden
keys: secret garden, silver bees, humming pear tree
canon: soft
text: Behind the potting shed, a door in the wall leads to Maud's secret garden: glowing ferns, silver bees and a pear tree that hums. It only exists for people Maud has shown it to.

@lore greenhouses
keys: greenhouses, moonflower
canon: soft
text: Glass houses that steam even in winter. The moonflowers there bloom once every eleven years and fill the greenhouse with silver light.

@lore observatory
keys: observatory, telescope, east tower
canon: soft
text: A brass dome atop the east tower. The great telescope points wherever it likes. On cold nights Kael sits on the roof outside it, and frost spreads around him.

@lore boathouse
keys: boathouse, jetty
canon: soft
text: An old boathouse with a jetty over the water, where people say the things they can't say indoors. The tunnel to the round door starts here.

@lore thornwick
keys: Thornwick Academy, rival school
canon: soft
text: The rival academy across the hills, famous for illusionists and tournament grudges. Exchange students come and go with suspicious politeness.

@lore the_north
keys: the North, Northern, ice palaces, singing glaciers, northern lights
canon: soft
text: The frozen North of ice palaces, singing glaciers and green-and-violet lights in the sky. Northerners touch foreheads in farewell and practise a frost-craft older than anything taught at Lumenhold.

@lore port_calder
keys: Port Calder, coast, street origin
canon: soft
text: A rough harbour town on the coast, where students of the street origin learned their trade and where trunks get stolen only once per visit.

@lore conclave
keys: Conclave, Conclave of the Seven Towers
canon: soft
text: The governing body of magic, in the capital. It asks professors for recommendations and runs laboratories where new spells are tested behind thick walls.

@lore capital_institutions
keys: Royal Library, Guild of Alchemists, Office of Unseen Affairs, Travelling Circus of Wonders
canon: soft
text: Beyond the academy lie the Royal Library's archives, the Guild of Alchemists' works, the Crown's Office of Unseen Affairs, which has no sign and no address, and the Travelling Circus of Wonders, which recruits graduates who want to wander.
